From: arcadematicas <arcadematicas@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: tolerate a NULL ar while a link is being torn down

The AYN Odin 3 (SM8750, WCN7860) panics within ~10 s of wlan0 coming up: the
AP stops answering, firmware commands start failing (-108), and the scan/link
teardown paths below dereference arvif->ar, which is not set for every link
still present in the links map. With oops=panic in the cmdline that is a boot
loop. Check arvif->ar before using it in the three paths that assume it.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -5927,7 +5927,7 @@
 
 	for_each_set_bit(link_id, &links_map, ATH12K_NUM_MAX_LINKS) {
 		arvif = wiphy_dereference(hw->wiphy, ahvif->link[link_id]);
-		if (!arvif || !arvif->is_created ||
+		if (!arvif || !arvif->is_created || !arvif->ar ||
 		    arvif->ar->scan.arvif != arvif)
 			continue;
 
@@ -11066,6 +11066,8 @@
 			continue;
 
 		ar = arvif->ar;
+		if (!ar)
+			continue;
 
 		/* Scan abortion is in progress since before this, cancel_hw_scan()
 		 * is expected to be executed. Since link is anyways going to be removed
@@ -12478,6 +12480,9 @@
 		return;
 
 	ar = arvif->ar;
+	if (!ar)
+		return;
+
 	ab = ar->ab;
 
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_MAC,
